        "body": "Ground truth is never error-free: field and laboratory measurements have their own uncertainty, detection limits and handling artefacts. Sampling units should match the satellite footprint or a documented sub-pixel design. Stratify across the gradient of interest (e.g. salinity, moisture) rather than clustering all points in one field. For dynamic variables, sample within days of the overpass and record GNSS accuracy. Replicate within pixels to quantify sub-pixel variability—one grab sample is not the pixel mean."
